Data Strategy and Governance Lead

Choosing Capgemini means choosing a company where you will be empowered to shape your career in the way you’d like, where you’ll be supported and inspired by a collaborative community of colleagues around the world, and where you’ll be able to reimagine what’s possible. Join us and help the world’s leading organizations unlock the value of technology and build a more sustainable, more inclusive world.

YOUR ROLE

As a Data Strategy and Governance Consultant, you will be a strategic partner to our clients, helping them establish and embed robust frameworks and processes to ensure effective data governance. This role combines advisory, strategy, and technical expertise, offering you the opportunity to contribute to building organizations that manage and leverage their data in a smart, efficient, and sustainable way.

In this role you will play a key role in:

- Design and implement best practices and frameworks for data governance, balancing business needs with regulatory requirements (based on DMBOK and EU AI Act);

- Advise clients on establishing a data governance structure, including designing roles such as data stewards and -owners;

- Contribute to creating a comprehensive data strategy, including establishing governance models for data architecture, data warehouses, and data catalogs;

- Assist in defining and structuring workflows for data quality, data control, and metadata management;

- Guide clients in implementing and adopting data mesh and other data governance approaches;

- Implement data quality rules and metrics; monitor and remediate;

-  Manage compliance with GDPR and EU AI Act (risk classification, documentation).

YOUR PROFILE

- At least 3-5 years of experience in data governance, data strategy, or related data management roles;

- Experience in structuring roles and responsibilities within data governance and establishing collaboration models across business and IT;

- A foundational understanding of data architecture, data warehousing and cloud solutions;

- Strong communication skills with the ability to explain technical concepts to both technical and non-technical stakeholders.

